# {{MODULE}} module

Generated by `spinx make:module {{MODULE}}`. This layout is enforced by the
Spinx kernel — see `SPINX_BUILD_SPEC.md` §5 for the full rationale.

- **Domain/** — entities, value objects, domain events, and repository
  *interfaces* only. Zero dependencies on Application or Infrastructure.
  If a class here needs to import anything from Infrastructure, that's a
  sign the logic belongs in Application instead.
- **Application/** — services that orchestrate domain logic, plus
  commands/queries if you're using a CQRS-style split. This layer depends
  on Domain, never directly on Infrastructure implementations (depend on
  the Domain repository interface, not the concrete class).
- **Infrastructure/** — concrete repository implementations, HTTP
  controllers/middleware, and persistence/migrations. This is the only
  layer allowed to know about the database, HTTP, or third-party services.

Routes and DI bindings for this module are registered exclusively in
`module.php` in this directory — that file is the only thing the kernel's
`ModuleLoader` reads.

## State safety (persistent-process runtimes)

RoadRunner and Swoole keep the process alive across many requests, so any
state that isn't reset between requests can leak from one user's request
into another's. Spinx handles most of this automatically:

- Every service you register in `module.php` is **request-scoped by
  default** — torn down and rebuilt fresh at the start of every request.
- If a service is genuinely stateless and safe to persist, mark it
  `#[Singleton]` (from `Spinx\Container\Attribute\Singleton`) to opt out.
- **Static properties are not covered by container scoping** — they live
  on the class itself, not a container-managed instance. Avoid mutable
  static properties in this module entirely; a custom PHPStan rule
  (`phpstan.neon` in the project root) will flag them.

